    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Webhook contract\n\npipeline/generateContent.py POSTs here after a render finishes:\n\n```\n{ story_number, story_file_name,\n  video_path, metadata_path,\n  duration_seconds, render_seconds }\n```\n\nConfigured as N8N_RENDER_WEBHOOK in .env.\n\nStory Paths falls back to building the paths from story_number, so a\nhand-fired {\"story_number\": 36} still publishes.\n\n**This workflow must be ACTIVE** or the production webhook is not registered.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2470,
        130
      ],
      "id": "cfea1411-3400-434c-95b4-9c86a77b4ca0",
      "name": "Sticky Note0"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Upload quota is the real ceiling\n\nvideos.insert costs 1,600 units against a 10,000/day default:\nabout **6 uploads per day**.\n\nThe 50-minute cron in ContentGeneration attempts ~28, so most runs 403 on\nquota. That is why both HTTP nodes have an error output routed to\nEmail Failure rather than ending the execution silently.\n\nDo not raise the cron rate to match the faster render.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 470,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        130,
        208
      ],
      "id": "e811f0a8-44ff-413a-8b02-63b3144b39a1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    }
